expectation e_2ea25e8cda4d2d78 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="litterae keeps expectations explicit" detail="litterae should keep project expectations in an authored expectations.susu sidecar so implementation evidence and intent can be reviewed together.";
expectation e_ee705788dc2f4a20 target=project subject=- status=proposed source="human:maintainer" title="litterae documents primary workflows" detail="litterae should describe the business or product workflows that matter most, then link those expectations to observed files, symbols, or workflows as evidence improves.";
expectation e_0cf9ce3bfb208414 target=project subject=- status=proposed source="human:maintainer" title="litterae records verification evidence" detail="litterae should record how important expectations are checked, such as tests, CI runs, manual reviews, policy checks, runtime traces, or release approvals.";
expectation e_25466c712a403a7c target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="litterae reacts to SIGTERM, not just SIGINT" detail="The server process must catch SIGTERM (sent by docker stop and systemd) alongside SIGINT and run the same graceful-shutdown path, since the deployed environment (susumu.dev) stops the container via SIGTERM, not Ctrl-C.";
expectation e_5989aadcf3a862fc target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:justin" title="mail app surfaces action failures via toast, not inline red text" detail="Compose send/save, contact save/delete, message snooze/nudge/download, and mailbox pagination failures show a dismissible bottom-of-screen toast (web/src/lib/Toast.svelte + toast.svelte.ts) instead of a per-component inline red <p>. Initial-page-load failures (mailbox list, message view) stay as persistent inline empty/error states on purpose -- a toast would auto-dismiss over a blank page with no explanation left behind.";
